  "summary": "Sarumen Chaseki (猿面茶席) is a historic Japanese tea house (chashitsu) located within the grounds of Nagoya Castle in Nagoya, Aichi Prefecture, Japan.",
  "description": "Sarumen Chaseki (猿面茶席) is a historic Japanese tea house (chashitsu) located within the grounds of Nagoya Castle in Nagoya, Aichi Prefecture, Japan. Together with the adjacent Bōgaku Chaseki (望嶽茶席), it forms the Sarumen-Bōgaku tea complex. The tea house is regarded as one of the notable surviving examples of traditional tea architecture associated with early Edo-period castle culture.",
